A multi-paragraph inline note in fenced code is the code's text, and a
markdown-demo's code pane shows its notes as written; both showed a marker
where the note had been lifted out.

```markdown
The claim[fn: First paragraph.

    Second paragraph.
] is followed by more text, and a labelled one[^b: One.

    Two.
].
```

A real one outside the code still works.[fn: Its first paragraph.

    Its second.
]

:::markdown-demo
The standard account is incomplete[^acct:

    The first objection.

    The second.
] in two ways.
:::

The paragraph after them prints.[fn: A single-paragraph note.]
